-- title:
--   Degree q-1 over the subfield generated by the modular unit
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime. Inside $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ consider the intermediate field $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)`, that is the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image, under the ring map `coeffEmb` induced by $\mathbb Q \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$, of `modularFunctionFieldFull (1 * q)`, itself the $\mathbb Q$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\mathbb Q)$ generated by the family `divisorExpansions (1 * q)`. Let $u \in F$ be the element given by the `coeffEmb`-image of `modularUnitSeries (1 * q)`, namely of $\Delta \cdot (\,\text{$q$-th $q$-expansion rescaling of }\Delta)^{-1}$, where $\Delta$ is `deltaSeries`, the product of the Laurent monomial $X$ with the power series `dedekindEtaUnitQ`, and the rescaling is `qExpand ℚ (1 * q)`; that this Laurent series lies in `modularFunctionFieldFull (1 * q)` is [`ModularCurve.modularUnitSeries_mem_modularFunctionFieldFull`](thm.html#ModularCurve.modularUnitSeries_mem_modularFunctionFieldFull), and its image then lies in $F$. The assertion is that the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-intermediate field generated by the single element $u^{-1}$ has $F$ as a module of rank exactly $q - 1$ (subtraction of natural numbers, the rank being a natural number). The level is written throughout as $1 \cdot q$.
--
--   This is the statement that the function field of $X_0(q)$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ has degree $q-1$ over the rational subfield generated by the modular unit $\Delta/\Delta_q$ (equivalently by its inverse), the modular unit having a single pole of order $q-1$ at one of the two cusps. It is used in the analysis of prolongations of places from level one to level $q$, in particular in the divisor-law and integrality statements for the residue of the inverse modular unit.
